# Line-ending policy for the Agentic AI course repo.
#
# Why this file exists: participants clone on Windows, macOS and Linux and run the
# same `bash scripts/...` commands. Without this, git's core.autocrlf on Windows
# checks shell scripts out with CRLF and bash fails with "\r: command not found"
# before VS Code is ever involved. .vscode/settings.json sets files.eol to "\n",
# but that only governs what the editor writes — this governs what git checks out.

# Default: let git detect text, and always check text out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Must be LF ------------------------------------------------------------
# Executed by bash (setup.sh, cleanup.sh, submit-lab.sh, langfuse-server.sh …)
*.sh            text eol=lf
# Notebook JSON: CRLF would break the indent=2 round-trip that keeps notebook
# diffs to three lines instead of two thousand (see CLAUDE.md).
*.ipynb         text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.env           text eol=lf
.env.example    text eol=lf

# --- Must be CRLF ----------------------------------------------------------
# Run by Windows PowerShell, often after a download-as-ZIP rather than a clone.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# --- Never normalize -------------------------------------------------------
*.pdf           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.mp3           binary
*.mp4           binary
